## Required conventions

Use `createBadRequestError(...)` for invalid evaluation/remapping input and
`createInternalError(...)` for malformed application runtime context.

Do not use plain errors where the application error contract applies.

Reuse matching common object/string helpers rather than recreating them.

Use `resolveRequireValue(mode)` when its exact draft/submit abstraction fits.

Preserve:

```js
async ({ payload, decisionContext }) => frontendPayload
async ({ payload, decisionContext, mode }) => storedPayload
```

Do not mutate inputs or add queries for data already in `decisionContext`.

If criterion remapping exists, `criterionIdMap` is exactly:

```text
Map<temporaryCriterionId, persistedCriterionId>
```

Use `Map.has/get`, and remap only criterion references owned by this payload.

If payload values belong to an Expression Domain, reuse the canonical
Expression Domain validation infrastructure.

Keep logic small, local and explicit. No generic one-use abstractions,
compatibility fallbacks or new dependencies without need.

